  "provenance": {
    "pattern": "halftime drum and bass: the tempo stays at 170 and the snare moves to the third beat, one backbeat a bar, so the groove is felt at 85",
    "knowledge": "public knowledge of the genre: the pattern as drummers, producers and tutorials commonly write it; no recording was sampled, transcribed from audio or mined",
    "note": "Two bars: kick on one and a pickup kick just before the next bar's one, snare only on beat three (step 8), a ghost before the second snare; eighth hats on the offbeat. The sub holds long notes, a step down in the second bar. This is also as near as the kitchen comes to dubstep's grid: dubstep is this pattern at 140, and 140 is out of every band."
  }
